    "created_at": "2022-06-27T07:38:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-27T07:38:11Z",
    "body": "> Would it be better to PR the content attribute definition to HTML, rather than define it in the Element Timing spec, while we're waiting for multi-implementer interest?\r\n\r\nI don’t know which is best. One the one hand, defining it in the Element Timing spec is less desirable if it requires monkeypatching — and also because it’s ultimately extra work because it would eventually need to be removed from the Element Timing spec and copied over to the HTML spec. On the other hand — as you mention — while we’re waiting for multi-implementer interest it’s good to have it in an actual spec rather than just in a patch in a PR branch.\r\n\r\nMaybe @domenic can give some guidance here.",
